\section{Two p-values, kept apart}{

\code{p_value} is the log-rank test's. The Cox model has p-values of its own, and
the one that goes with the hazard ratio's interval is the Wald test's. It is
in \code{rows} as \code{hr_p_value}, labelled by \code{hr_test}, and is a different test
from the log-rank test: the two are usually close and need not agree.
}

\section{Censor flag or event flag}{

The outcome is a time and a flag, and the flag can be written either way
round. Say which by the argument used: \code{strCensorCol} names a column that is
1 for a censored time and 0 for an event, as ADaM's \code{CNSR} is;
\code{strEventCol} names a column that is 1 (or \code{TRUE}) for an event and 0 (or
\code{FALSE}) for a censored time. Exactly one must be given, and a column
holding anything but 0 and 1 is refused. The first of \code{notes} states which
value was read as an event, and \code{rows} gives the events in each group, so a
flag read the wrong way round shows.
}

